WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.334 line:14%
 My name's Kevin Adams.

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.903 line:8%
I am a technical instructor
for the United States Army,

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.471 line:14%
and I'm a part time bladesmith.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.208
My grandfather and my father
worked in the same steel mill

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.511
together, so their influence
enabled me to be able to pick

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.746
up the trade fairly quickly.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.849 line:8%
 My name is Aric Fontaine
and I have been bladesmithing

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.218 line:14%
now for almost 10 years.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.454
I stay with it because it's
a comfort place for me.

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.724
And just being able
to create something,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.959
it's a really cool experience.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.394
 Well, Kevin, Aric,
congratulations.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.329
You guys are both moving
forward into round three

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.931
of our competition,
where we will

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.301
be sending you home to work on
an iconic weapon from history.

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:41.507
And that weapon is the
serrated Tegha sword.

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:44.410
 Lord have mercy.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.979
NARRATOR: Originating in
India in the 18th century,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.881
this intimidating
curved sword was known

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.783
to be a great executioner.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.920
Its unique design features a
nearly three foot long blade

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.155
with a split tip
and serrated edges

00:00:56.221 --> 00:00:58.224
that could easily behead a man.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.293
Its two pronged tip
is a powerful symbol

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.796
throughout the Islamic
world and is inspired

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.198
by the legendary
sword Zulfiqar, which

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:08.935
is believed to be descended
from the prophet Muhammad.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.135
 You guys have a
lot of parameters

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.205
to follow, so pay attention.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.839
You guys need to
make a blade that

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.609
is between 24 and 26 inches.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.180
That curve depth needs to be
no less than 3 and 1/2 inches.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.850
You need to have a split at the
tip that goes down between 10

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.686
and 11 inches, followed
by a puncture hole

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.288
at the end of that split.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.790
The curved edge and the
back edge of the split

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.991
need to be serrated
and sharpened.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.393
Now you guys need
to have a Khanda

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:37.030
style hilt with a tail pommel.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.832
 I have never seen anything
like this in my life.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.200
It's got these crazy curves.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.501
It's serrated everywhere.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.104
It just combines so many
different skill sets.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.106
It's going to be a
challenge to create.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.108
 You have four days
in your home forges.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.377
We'll see you then.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.144
 Good luck.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.113
 Good luck to you as well.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:01.087
 I'm back in my home forge
and I'm ready to start

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:02.889
working on this serrated Tegha.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.623
The length and the
curvature of the blade

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.527
is something I've never
had to deal with before.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.763
Start getting my
blade forged to shape.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.765
Looks like a hockey stick.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.667
So now I got to shape the tip.

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:17.170
That's concerning for me
because the only thing I have

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.038
to cut metal with is a grinder.

00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:20.840
You don't have a lot of control.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.342
Not pretty, but it's a start.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.145
Getting ready to
quench the blade.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:28.781
She's hard.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.283
The heat treat went good.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:34.654
There's a lot of work to do
yet, but it's a good start.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.558
The plan for today is make that
cut from the hole to the tip.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.060
This is a butt
puckering moment for me.

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:43.062
If this doesn't work,
I'm in deep trouble.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.832
Oh man, that is way
too thin up there.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.166
What can you do?

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.036
Now my biggest challenge
is the handle and guard.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.837
There's a lot of
moving parts with it.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:54.874
Even though it's a lot of hard
work and there's frustration,

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:55.841
I had fun.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.243
That's why we do this craft.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.249
 It's good to be back
here in my own domain.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.352
I'm going to be building
a serrated Tegha sword.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:08.521
I've never done anything
even remotely close to it,

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.090
so it's going to be
an exciting build.

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.592
I got the rough shape on my tip.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.360
I'm going to take
it over to the vise

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.261
and I'm going to start
splitting it down.

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:18.130
While my steel is
heating, I might as well

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.499
be doing something else.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:20.833
This is going to be the guard.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.835
I grab the metal that
I'm going to be using

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.237
for my pommel and the guard.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.506
I start forging those into
the proper dimensions.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:29.141
Right now, I feel like
I'm in pretty good shape.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.678
Time to quench.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:34.847
It's actually not bad.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:37.183
It's time to
assemble this thing.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.384
All right.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.953
That's a little
better, less worse.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.855
Now that I have
a finished blade,

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.625
I have a piece of roast beef.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:49.261
That is a nice, clean
cut right there.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.798
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.499
Let's find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.434
your serrated Tegha will do.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.602
Kevin, you're up first.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.302
You ready?

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:58.237
 Ready as I'll ever be.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.605
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.273
 As Doug is getting
ready to do the kill test,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.275
I can feel my heart
rate is increasing.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.111
Is there a flaw
in there anywhere?

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.278
Did I heat treat correct?

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:09.181
So I'm feeling not
that confident.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:14.754
[music playing]

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:29.969
 All right.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.671
Kevin, let's talk about
your serrated Tegha here.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:33.372
First up, the
serrations you have here

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.007
are indeed very sharp.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:36.476
You can feel every cut.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.611
Now your handle
construction is smooth.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.612
A little bit on the
wider side of this

00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:44.017
handle, but it wasn't an issue
in controlling your weapon.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.587
Overall, sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:48.721
All right, Aric.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.589
Ready to take a look?

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:51.924
 I'm ready.
Let's do it.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.259
DOUG: All right.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.561
 Kevin's blade performed
absolutely phenomenal.

00:04:55.627 --> 00:04:57.063
I mean, he cut the
dummy's head off.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:00.399
I've got to perform at least
at that level to even have

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:04.102
a chance at winning this thing.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:09.075
[music playing]

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:20.853
 All right, Aric.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.922
The serrations on
your sword are sharp.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:26.158
When I ripped through the
shoulder, it cut easily.

00:05:26.224 --> 00:05:29.128
Now your sword is much lighter.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.230
It tapers before it
gets to the bend,

00:05:31.296 --> 00:05:34.100
making the sword easy
to swing one handed.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.636
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will kill.

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.639
 Awesome.

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:43.176
 All right, gentlemen,
time for the strength test.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.611
Now to test the strength
and overall construction

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:48.748
of your blades, I will be taking
them and smashing these pots.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.517
Now remember, this is not
about how well your blades hold

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:52.885
up through this punishment.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:53.719
Kevin, you're up first.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:54.320
You ready?

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.188
 Yes, sir.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.426
[music playing]

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:10.736
 Kevin, your handle,
it's kind of fat.

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.739
But your distance, your
scale with your guard

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:14.706
is great for me.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.274
As far as your
blade goes, I mean,

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.444
you've taken some
pretty big hits

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.880
and lost a lot of the
tips of your serrations.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.149
The blade is in one piece.

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:24.183
It's still solid.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.084
Nothing loosened up.

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:25.818
Well done.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:26.785
 Thank you.

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:27.486
 All right.

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:28.920
Aric, ready to get ugly?

00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:30.922
 Tear it up.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:36.028
[music playing]

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.878
 I wasn't expecting sparks.

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:55.314
 So Aric, right off,
up here on your blade,

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.549
you've taken some damage
on these serrations.

00:06:57.649 --> 00:06:58.984
You lost a bit of this edge.

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.153
It's still in one piece.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.787
You did a good job.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:02.721
Congratulations.

00:07:02.821 --> 00:07:04.957
 Thank you.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.359
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.527
It's time to find out how
sharp your blades are.

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:11.630
This is the sharpness
test, the jackfruit slice.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.299
To find out how sharp
your weapons are,

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.200
I'm going to take your
weapon to cut the rope

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.435
and release this jackfruit.

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.337
Then I'm going to
slice through it.

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.605
Now unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.974
is all about what the
edge of your blade

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.109
does to the jackfruit.

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:24.943
Kevin, you're up first.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:25.744
You ready?

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:26.378
 Yes, sir.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:29.014
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:34.120
[music playing]

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.801
All right, Kevin, let's
talk about your edge here.

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:53.105
So the sweet spot that we
have right here for this sword

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:56.108
took a lot of damage
during the strength test.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:59.278
So in the initial cut on
the rope, it didn't cut.

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:02.581
Now on the second cut, we
used a little bit other parts

00:08:02.647 --> 00:08:04.416
of the blade where it is sharp.

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:06.719
It cut the rope and
it cut the jackfruit.

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:09.755
So overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:11.022
- Good.
- All right, Aric.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:11.791
Your turn, sir.

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:12.391
Are you ready?

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.159
 Let's do it.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:19.165
[music playing]

00:08:26.438 --> 00:08:27.239
 All right, Aric.

00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:28.607
So it's the same thing.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.609
The sweet spot on this
blade took some dulling

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.010
on the strength test.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.946
It did affect cutting the
rope on the first attempt.

00:08:34.012 --> 00:08:36.482
On the second attempt,
cut that rope and it

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:38.417
also cut the jackfruit in half.

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:41.086
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:43.055
 Excellent.

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:45.590
 Well, gentlemen, we gave you
an extremely difficult blade

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.559
to build in the Tegha
sword, and you both

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:49.428
performed exceptionally
well in our tests.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.930
But the judges have
made the decision,

00:08:50.997 --> 00:08:52.498
and there can only
be one champion.

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:57.335
And the "Forged in Fire"
champion today is Aric.

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:58.670
Congratulations.

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:00.139
Kevin, unfortunately,
you didn't make the cut,

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.439
and Dave's going
to tell you why.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.009
 Kevin, what this
came down to was

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:06.312
the heat treat in that blade,
not getting it hard enough.

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:08.180
And so many of
those teeth just got

00:09:08.246 --> 00:09:10.116
pounded back into that blade.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.316
That's why we're letting you go.

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:12.617
 OK.

00:09:12.717 --> 00:09:14.019
 Well, Kevin, you did
exceptionally well,

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:15.921
but unfortunately your time
in the forge has ended.

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:18.557
I'm going to have to ask
you to please step out.

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:20.426
 That was probably
the most challenging

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:21.960
thing that I've ever done.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.397
It had about half a dozen things
that I'd never done before.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.532
I gave it my all, so
I'm pleased with what

00:09:26.599 --> 00:09:27.767
I've brought to the table.

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:31.503
And I'm ready to get
back at it again.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:32.738
 Aric, congratulations.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.441
You are today's "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:35.508 --> 00:09:36.308
Feeling pretty good?

00:09:36.408 --> 00:09:37.342
 I'm feeling amazing.

00:09:37.442 --> 00:09:38.377
 You definitely impressed us.

00:09:38.444 --> 00:09:39.778
Good job, man.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.746
Without further ado, there
is a check for $10,000

00:09:41.846 --> 00:09:43.015
waiting for you out that door.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:43.816
Go grab it.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:44.984
 Thank you.

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:47.085
I don't even know
how it happened.

00:09:47.152 --> 00:09:48.154
Oh man.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.089
That is, it's a surreal feeling.

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:51.423
Still hasn't even kicked in.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.891
I recently got engaged.

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:56.095
So I will be putting the
$10,000 towards my wedding

00:09:56.195 --> 00:09:57.996
and my honeymoon afterwards.

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.398
Love you, baby.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.801
[music playing]

